"""
A pointer to an entity that contains a page, carrying only what a client needs in
order to identify and label it.

Deliberately terminal: it exposes no `contents` or any other traversal field, so it
cannot be used to walk back into the site tree. This is what stops a page read from
turning into an unbounded site-tree traversal (Page -> Folder -> contents -> Page).
Fetch `HelpCenterFolder` by `id` if you need the full entity.
"""
type HelpCenterPageParentReference {
  """
  Identifier of the parent entity. This is an ARI, whose resource type varies with
  `type` - e.g. `ari:cloud:help::folder/<uuid>` when `type` is `FOLDER`.
  
  Intentionally NOT annotated with `@ARI(type: "folder", ...)`: that directive pins
  a single resource type, and this identifier is polymorphic by design.
  """
  id: ID!
  """
  Display name of the parent, already locale-resolved.
  
  Non-null: the only nameless node in the site tree is the invisible ROOT folder,
  and ROOT is excluded from this chain.
  """
  name: String!
  """
  Which kind of entity this parent is. Always `FOLDER` today. Tells the client how
  to interpret `id` and which schema type it resolves to.
  """
  type: HelpCenterPageParentType!
}

