"Hypothesis details for an indicator of type HYPOTHESIS."
type HypothesisIndicator {
  "A human-readable summary of the hypothesis."
  hypothesisSummary: String
  "The type of hypothesis."
  hypothesisType: MitigationHypothesisType
  "Direct link to the hypothesis in its source system, when one is available."
  link: String
  "The sources that this hypothesis was derived from."
  provenance: [IndicatorProvenance!]
}

"""
One hypothesis from an RCA investigation, the state of its mitigation plan generation, and the
plans produced for it.

Generation is asynchronous: the mutation returns as soon as the hypothesis is durable, and the
caller polls one of the queries until `state` reports a terminal type.

Deliberately separate from `Mitigation` and its types. That family models a whole incident's
mitigation run and fans out across every indicator; this models the one hypothesis a user picked.
The two are read by different screens and evolve independently.
"""
type HypothesisMitigation implements Node @defaultHydration(batchSize : 90, field : "playbook_hypothesisMitigations", idArgument : "ids", identifiedBy : "id", timeout : -1) {
  "The investigation's confidence in this hypothesis, as reported upstream."
  confidenceScore: String
  createdAt: String
  """
  Identifies the hypothesis within that investigation. This is `rootCauseSuggestionId` in the
  AIOps RCA contract, named here as it is named in ours.
  """
  hypothesisId: String
  "Relay Node id (ARI) of the underlying mitigation indicator."
  id: ID! @ARI(interpreted : false, owner : "jira", type : "playbook-mitigation-indicator", usesActivationId : false)
  "The investigation the hypothesis was resolved from."
  investigationId: String
  "The mitigation run this hypothesis belongs to, as a Relay Node id (ARI)."
  mitigationId: ID @ARI(interpreted : false, owner : "jira", type : "playbook-mitigation", usesActivationId : false)
  "Plans generated for this hypothesis. Empty until generation completes."
  plans: [HypothesisMitigationPlan!]
  """
  Knowledge sources behind this hypothesis, consolidated from the indicator's provenance and its
  plans' sources, deduplicated.
  """
  sources: [HypothesisMitigationSource!]
  "Progress of plan generation. Null only when the driving request cannot be read."
  state: HypothesisMitigationState
  title: String
  updatedAt: String
}

"""
One incident's hypothesis mitigation, together with what the calling user may do to it.

Returned by `playbook_hypothesisMitigationOverviewByScope`, which supersedes
`playbook_hypothesisMitigationsByScope` — that returned the summaries alone, leaving a caller no way to
learn the user's authority without attempting a mutation. Every field is resolved only when selected.

The permissions hang off the incident rather than off `Mitigation` because `canCreateMitigation` has to
be answerable before a mitigation exists, which is exactly when a client needs it.

**The permissions are advisory.** Every mutation independently enforces the same check, so an
optimistic `true` cannot grant access. A mutation refused this way fails with
`errorType: "MITIGATION_PERMISSION_DENIED"` and status 403, distinct from the general
`PLAYBOOK_FORBIDDEN_ERROR`. Per the ICC permission DACI, use these to explain state, not to disable or
hide a call to action.

**A tenant that permission checking is not switched on for reports every permission as `true`**, since
nothing is denied while nothing is checked. Do not read `true` as proof that a role was verified.
"""
type HypothesisMitigationOverview {
  "Whether the calling user may add a step to a mitigation plan on this incident. Null means no decision could be reached; treat it as permitted, which is what the server does, and let the mutation refuse if it must."
  canAddMitigationStep: Boolean
  "Whether the calling user may set a mitigation plan's assignee on this incident. Decided by the same ICC action as `canCreateMitigation`."
  canAssignMitigationPlan: Boolean
  "Whether the calling user may have a mitigation plan generated for a hypothesis on this incident. Null means no decision could be reached; treat it as permitted, which is what the server does, and let the mutation refuse if it must."
  canCreateMitigation: Boolean
  "Whether the calling user may remove a step from a mitigation plan on this incident. Decided by the same ICC action as `canAddMitigationStep`, so the two agree today, but read the one matching the control you render."
  canDeleteMitigationStep: Boolean
  "Whether the calling user may run a mitigation plan step on this incident. Decided by the same ICC action as the read of the plan itself, since the permission API has no execute action: a user who may not see a plan may not run its steps, but anyone who may see one is reported as able to run them. Treat this as a floor rather than proof the user holds a responder role. Null means no decision could be reached; treat it as permitted, which is what the server does, and let the mutation refuse if it must."
  canExecuteMitigationStep: Boolean
  "The hypotheses on the incident that mitigation has been requested for. Persisted hypotheses only, so one the investigation produced but nobody acted on does not appear. Empty when mitigation has never been requested."
  hypotheses: [HypothesisMitigationSummary!]
}

"A plan generated for a hypothesis."
type HypothesisMitigationPlan implements Node @defaultHydration(batchSize : 90, field : "playbook_hypothesisMitigationPlans", idArgument : "ids", identifiedBy : "id", timeout : -1) {
  "The user this plan is assigned to, or null when unassigned."
  assignee: User @hydrated(arguments : [{name : "accountIds", value : "$source.assigneeAccountId"}], batchSize : 50, field : "users", identifiedBy : "accountId", indexed : false, inputIdentifiedBy : [], service : "identity", timeout : -1)
  "Confidence bucket for this plan, or null when it was drawn from no scored source."
  confidence: HypothesisMitigationConfidence
  createdAt: String
  "Relay Node id (ARI) of the plan. Null if the activation id cannot be resolved."
  id: ID! @ARI(interpreted : false, owner : "jira", type : "playbook-mitigation-plan", usesActivationId : false)
  """
  The playbook this plan was mirrored to, as an ARI, matching `JiraPlaybook.id` on the legacy
  create-playbook response. Null if the activation id cannot be resolved.
  """
  playbookId: ID @ARI(interpreted : false, owner : "jira", type : "playbook", usesActivationId : false)
  """
  The plan's steps, in the order they should be carried out. Read from the mirrored Jira Playbook
  rather than from the plan, so they carry server-minted step ids and reflect any edits a user has
  since made to that playbook. Resolved only when requested.
  """
  steps: [HypothesisMitigationPlanStep!]
  summary: String
  """
  `summary` as ADF: its own source ADF document when one exists, otherwise `summary` itself
  wrapped as plain-text ADF. Null only when `summary` is.
  """
  summaryAdf: JSON @suppressValidationRule(rules : ["JSON"])
  title: String
}

"""
One step of a plan.

Shaped to match `JiraPlaybookStep`, because it is one: every plan is mirrored to a Jira Playbook
when it is persisted, and these are that playbook's steps. A caller can therefore hand a step
straight to the playbook APIs without translating it.
"""
type HypothesisMitigationPlanStep {
  """
  What executing this step does, phrased for a button or a heading — "Pause the problematic feature
  gate". Null exactly when `actionType` is, so a caller can rely on the pair. Free of the artefact
  it acts on, which `name` already carries: repeating it would put the same url in front of a reader
  twice. Fixed per action rather than read from the step, so it does not change once a run starts.
  """
  actionTitle: String
  """
  The action executing this step performs, or null when the step supports none. Set only for a plan
  built deterministically from an artefact the investigation blamed, and resolved per plan so a
  hypothesis blaming both a code change and a feature gate publishes the right action on each. A
  plan extracted by the LLM carries none, because there is nothing for it to act on.
  """
  actionType: HypothesisMitigationActionType
  """
  Whether a responder has marked this step done. Nullable at the schema layer; when present,
  an unmarked step reports done: false. Independent of stepExecutions — a revert action raises
  a draft pull request, and only the responder knows whether it was merged, so a successful action
  does not mark the step done.
  """
  completion: HypothesisMitigationStepCompletion
  "ADF document, as on `JiraPlaybookStep.description`."
  description: JSON @suppressValidationRule(rules : ["JSON"])
  """
  The step's most recent run, or null if it has never been run. Shaped to match
  JiraPlaybookStepRun so a caller can render it with whatever it already uses for playbook runs.
  """
  lastRun: HypothesisMitigationStepRun
  name: String
  """
  Sub-steps from the step's latest action execution, or null if it has never been executed.
  Currently empty on mark-as-done responses; LLD expects rows to persist instead.
  """
  stepExecutions: [HypothesisMitigationStepExecution!]
  """
  Server-minted id of the step on the mirrored playbook, addressed under the scope the mitigation
  was raised for. Stable across plan reads.
  """
  stepId: ID! @ARI(interpreted : false, owner : "jira", type : "playbook-instance-step", usesActivationId : false)
  type: HypothesisMitigationStepType
}

"One step of the generation pipeline, as reached for this hypothesis."
type HypothesisMitigationProgressStep {
  completedAt: String
  "Why this step failed, when it did."
  failureReason: String
  startedAt: String
  step: String!
  stepStatus: String
}

"A knowledge source behind a hypothesis or its plans."
type HypothesisMitigationSource {
  "ARI of the source, when it has one."
  ari: String
  link: String
  "Product-line classification. Null when the underlying source type does not map to one."
  type: HypothesisMitigationSourceType
}

"How far plan generation has got for one hypothesis."
type HypothesisMitigationState {
  "Why generation failed. Populated only when `type` is FAILED."
  failureReason: String
  "Each pipeline step reached so far, oldest first."
  steps: [HypothesisMitigationProgressStep!]
  type: HypothesisMitigationStateType
}

"Whether a responder has marked a plan step done."
type HypothesisMitigationStepCompletion {
  """
  False for a step nobody has marked, so a caller never has to handle an absent completion.
  Nullable at the schema layer so a resolver error surfaces as a null field rather than
  destroying the parent step; the "never null in practice" guarantee is enforced in the
  service, not here.
  """
  done: Boolean
  "When the step was marked done; null when nobody has."
  doneAt: DateTime
  "The user who marked the step done, hydrated from doneByAccountId."
  doneBy: User @hydrated(arguments : [{name : "accountIds", value : "$source.doneByAccountId"}], batchSize : 50, field : "users", identifiedBy : "id", indexed : false, inputIdentifiedBy : [], service : "identity", timeout : -1)
  "Account id of whoever marked the step done; null when nobody has."
  doneByAccountId: String
}

"One run of a plan step."
type HypothesisMitigationStepExecution {
  "When this substep began, for ordering substeps within an execution."
  startedAt: DateTime
  "Current execution state."
  status: HypothesisMitigationStepExecutionStatus
  "The executed plan step, as an ADF document."
  step: JSON! @suppressValidationRule(rules : ["JSON"])
}

"What a run produced, copied from JiraPlaybookStepOutput."
type HypothesisMitigationStepOutput {
  message: String
  results: [HypothesisMitigationStepOutputKeyValuePair!]
}

"A single result of a run, copied from JiraPlaybookStepOutputKeyValuePair."
type HypothesisMitigationStepOutputKeyValuePair {
  key: String
  value: String
}

"""
One run of a plan step, shaped to match JiraPlaybookStepRun field for field. It is not a Node:
a run is only ever delivered inline with its step, and the playbook-step-run ARI is already
claimed by JiraPlaybookStepRun, so node(id) could not tell the two apart. Its id is still a
playbook-step-run ARI at runtime, but is left undeclared because declaring it would oblige this
type to be a Node.
"""
type HypothesisMitigationStepRun {
  completedAt: DateTime
  contextId: ID @ARI(interpreted : false, owner : "jira", type : "issue", usesActivationId : false)
  errorType: String
  id: ID!
  issue: JiraIssue @hydrated(arguments : [{name : "ids", value : "$source.contextId"}], batchSize : 50, field : "jira.issuesById", identifiedBy : "id", indexed : false, inputIdentifiedBy : [], service : "gira", timeout : -1)
  playbookId: ID
  playbookName: String
  ruleId: String
  stepDuration: Long
  stepId: ID
  stepName: String
  stepOutput: [HypothesisMitigationStepOutput!]
  stepStatus: HypothesisMitigationStepRunStatus
  stepType: HypothesisMitigationStepType
  taskId: ID @ARI(interpreted : false, owner : "jira", type : "issue", usesActivationId : false)
  triggeredAt: DateTime
  triggeredBy: User @hydrated(arguments : [{name : "accountIds", value : "$source.triggeredByAccountId"}], batchSize : 50, field : "users", identifiedBy : "id", indexed : false, inputIdentifiedBy : [], service : "identity", timeout : -1)
  triggeredByAccountId: String
}

"""
A hypothesis on an incident that mitigation has been requested for. Deliberately thin: enough to
list what is under way and to address any one of them, without reading each one's plans.
"""
type HypothesisMitigationSummary {
  "The hypothesis' upstream id, as issued by the investigation."
  hypothesisId: String
  "The investigation the hypothesis belongs to."
  investigationId: String
  """
  That investigation's place in the incident's re-run sequence, as the investigation service formatted
  it: "v1" for the original run, "v2" for the first re-run. Null when the hypothesis carries no
  version; render its absence rather than inferring one.
  """
  investigationVersion: String
  "One-line statement of what the hypothesis claims."
  summary: String
}

