  "The account ID of the agent assigned to the session."
  agentAccountId: String
  "The ARI of the studio agent for this session."
  agentAri: ID @ARI(interpreted : false, owner : "rovo", type : "agent", usesActivationId : false)
  "The user who initiated the agent session."
  author: User @hydrated(arguments : [{name : "accountIds", value : "$source.authorAccountId"}], batchSize : 90, field : "users", identifiedBy : "accountId", indexed : false, inputIdentifiedBy : [], service : "identity", timeout : -1)
  "The account ID of the user who initiated the agent session."
  authorAccountId: String
  "The Convo AI agent identifier backing this session."
  convoAiAgentId: String
  "The time when the agent session ended, if applicable."
  endTime: DateTime
  "The type of invocation that triggered the agent session."
  invocationType: JiraAgentSessionInvocationType
  "Whether the agent is a Rovo agent."
  isRovo: Boolean
  "The ARI of the associated JCA (Jira Coding Agent) session, if one exists."
  jcaSessionAri: ID
  "The time when the agent session state was last changed."
  lastStateChangeAt: DateTime
  """
  The time when the agent session state was last changed.
  
  
  This field is **deprecated** and will be removed in the future
  """
  lastStateChangedAt: DateTime
  "The URL of the pull request created by the session."
  pullRequestUrl: String
  """
  This agent session reshaped as the AgentSessionAssociation the work item view reads from
  JiraIssue.agentSessions.connection, so consumers can share fragments across both surfaces. The
  issue table needs this on the field because it must request values through
  JiraIssueEdge.fieldSets rather than JiraIssue directly.
  
  Derived in memory from the same Agent Sessions field value that backs this session, so it adds
  no read. Two fields have no counterpart in the field value: deleted is always false, because
  dismissed associations are removed from it, and subEntityId is not carried at all.
  
  Null when the owning work item is unknown, which is the case for a session nested inside an
  association.
  """
