"Represents a workflow in a Jira board view."
type JiraBoardViewWorkflow {
  """
  Exact project and issue type pairs associated with this workflow in this board, in this column or cell.
  Use it to select the workflow of an issue from its project and issue type, for example when the user
  starts dragging a card.
  
  Describes which workflow applies, not whether a particular issue can be transitioned. Use
  `JiraBoardView.availableTransitionsForIssues` for that.
  
  Ordered by project key, then issue type.
  """
  associations(
    """
    The index based cursor to specify the beginning of the items.
    If not specified it's assumed as the cursor for the item before the beginning.
    """
    after: String,
    """
    The number of items after the cursor to be returned in a forward page.
    If not specified, it is up to the server to determine a page size.
    """
    first: Int
  ): JiraBoardViewWorkflowAssociationConnection
  """
  Whether the requesting user can edit this workflow. False when the workflow is shared across
  multiple projects, even if the user has the EDIT_WORKFLOW project permission, because editing
  a shared workflow requires admin rights.
  """
  canEdit: Boolean
  """
  Transitions of this workflow into the statuses of the parent status column or cell.
  
  In a status column (`JiraBoardViewStatusColumn.mappedWorkflows`), these are all transitions of the
  workflow into the column's statuses, including DIRECTED transitions, for moving issues between columns.
  Whether a transition applies to a particular issue also depends on its current status and conditions;
  use `JiraBoardView.availableTransitionsForIssues` for that.
  
  In a cell, these are only initial OR global and unconditional transitions, used for creating issues
  in the board.
  """
  eligibleTransitions(
    """
    The index based cursor to specify the beginning of the items.
    If not specified it's assumed as the cursor for the item before the beginning.
    """
    after: String,
    """
    The number of items after the cursor to be returned in a forward page.
    If not specified, it is up to the server to determine a page size.
    """
    first: Int,
    "Whether to include restricted transitions. The default is `false`, i.e. to not include restricted transitions."
    includeRestricted: Boolean
  ): JiraTransitionConnection
  "Opaque ID uniquely identifying this node."
  id: ID!
  """
  Issue types creatable from this workflow on this board, scoped to the user. Each entry carries the
  set of fields the user can set when inline-creating an issue of this type from this board
  (issue-type schema ∩ user permissions ∩ board-surfaced inline pickers).
  """
  inlineCreatableIssueTypes: [JiraBoardViewInlineCreatableIssueType!]
  """
  Issue types associated with this workflow, across all projects of the board.
  The same issue type can use a different workflow in another project; use `associations` for the
  exact project and issue type pairs.
  """
  issueTypes(
    """
    The index based cursor to specify the beginning of the items.
    If not specified it's assumed as the cursor for the item before the beginning.
    """
    after: String,
    """
    The number of items after the cursor to be returned in a forward page.
    If not specified, it is up to the server to determine a page size.
    """
    first: Int
  ): JiraIssueTypeConnection
  "Name of the workflow."
  name: String
  "Entity ID of the workflow."
  workflowEntityId: ID!
}

