  The field is extremely unstable. It can go through changes at any moment, and its execution can be slow and/or unreliable. Clients should use it with care and at their own risk!
  """
  associatedIssueTypes(after: String, first: Int, input: JiraFieldSchemeAssociatedIssueTypesInput): JiraIssueTypeConnection @lifecycle(allowThirdParties : false, name : "JiraFieldSchemeAssociatedIssueTypes", stage : EXPERIMENTAL) @scopes(product : JIRA, required : [JIRA_ATLASSIAN_EXTERNAL]) @scopes(product : JIRA, required : [READ_JIRA_WORK])
  "Returns Projects associated with a given Field Scheme."
  associatedProjects(after: String, first: Int, input: JiraAssociatedProjectSearchInput): JiraProjectConnection
  "Returns Projects available to be associated with a given Field Scheme."
  availableProjects(after: String, first: Int, input: JiraAvailableProjectSearchInput): JiraProjectConnection
  description: String
  fieldsCount: Int
  id: ID! @ARI(interpreted : false, owner : "jira", type : "field-scheme", usesActivationId : false)
  "Marking the default scheme which cannot be deleted or have its name edited"
  isDefault: Boolean
  name: String
  projectsCount: Int
  """
  Returns the issue types, the fields of this field scheme are required on.
  
  ### OAuth Scopes
  
  One of the following scopes will need to be present on OAuth requests to get data from this field
  
  * __jira:atlassian-external__
  * __read:jira-work__
  
