"Response payload for the jira_setDefaultPolicy mutation."
type JiraSetDefaultPolicyPayload implements Payload {
  "A list of errors that occurred during the mutation, if any."
  errors: [MutationError!]
  """
  The policy that lost default status as a result of this mutation, as it stands after the change.
  Because only one policy can be the default, its isDefault field is always false.
  Null when the mutation displaced nothing: when no policy was the default beforehand, when the
  target policy already held the requested value, and when the mutation was unsuccessful. When the
  target policy itself was unset as the default, this is that policy.
  """
  previousDefaultPolicy: JiraProjectPolicy
  "Whether the mutation was successful."
  success: Boolean!
  """
  The policy targeted by the mutation, as stored after the change. Its isDefault field reflects
  the requested value. Null if the mutation was unsuccessful.
  """
  updatedPolicy: JiraProjectPolicy
}

