Site-level feature toggles for the given product on the given site. Extensible container: add
new site-level features as sibling fields here. Each field is resolved lazily, so a downstream
call is only made for the features a client actually requests.
eslint-disable-next-line @graphql-eslint/strict-id-in-types -- id is not required
"""
type MarketplaceStoreSiteFeaturesResponse {
  """
  Whether AI (the "AI Switch") is enabled for the input product on the input site, per the
  AI Enabled App Policy (proxies Identity Platform's `read:features:ai` permission). Returns
  `null` when this is unknown (unsupported product, no user context, or a downstream error) —
  callers should treat `null` the same as "enabled" (fail open) since this is used for a
  non-blocking install-flow nudge, not an enforcement check.
  """
  aiEnabled: Boolean
}

"""
Top-level response for `marketplaceStore.siteInfo`.

`hasErrors` follows the same semantics as on
`MarketplaceStoreUserSitesResult` — true when the per-site enrichment call
(TCS + Identity bulk/permitted) failed for the returned site. `site` is
still emitted on enrichment errors (with affected fields set to null) so
the frontend can render a degraded UX.

When the user has no access to the requested site (or no sites at all when
no input is supplied), `site` is null and `hasErrors` is false.
"""
type MarketplaceStoreSiteInfoResult {
  """
  True when the per-site enrichment call (TCS or Identity) reported an
  error. When `site` is null this is always false (nothing to enrich).
  """
  hasErrors: Boolean!
  "The single enriched site, or null when access cannot be confirmed."
  site: MarketplaceStoreUserSite
}

